
Island Models. 

Steps:

0. R-Profiles:

     rmpiProfile.R

The results will be stored in the four existing 
directories

mpiHetResult, mpiHomResult,
rdsHetResult, rdsHomResult.

The script cleanDirectories.sh deletes all files in this directories.

======================

1. Generate StartConfigurations.

   Rscript buildTSPlin105.R

    generates two configuration files:

1a. TSPlin105HomConfig.rds  for homogeneous islands
1b. TSPlin105Het4Config.rds for heterogeneous islands

   And cleanup directories for results.

   ./cleanDirectories.sh

2. Scripts for mpi.

2A. Batch scripts.

    The R-script must load the R-profile rmpiProfile.R    

2Aa. For homogeneous islands:

    ./mpiRun.sh mpiTSPlin105Hom.R

    ./mpiRun.sh mpiTSPlin105HomAdapt.R

    Results in directory mpiHomResult

2Ab. For heterogeneous islands:

    ./mpiRun.sh mpiTSPlin105Het.R

    Results in directory mpiHetResult

2B. Start scripts in 4 terminals.

2Ba. For homogeneous islands:

    ./mpiTerminals.sh mpiTSPlin105Hom.R

2Bb. For heterogeneous islands:
Rscript buildTSPlin105.R
    ./mpiTerminals.sh mpiTSPlin105Het.R

    ./mpiTerminals.sh mpiTSPlin105HetAdapt.R
    ./mpiTerminals.sh mpiTSPlin105HetAdaptOptimist.R

    ./mpiTerminals.sh mpiTSPlin105HetEarly.R

    Blocking:     

   ./mpiTerminals.sh mpibTSPlin105Het.R

3. Scripts for rds

3A. Batch scripts.
    - R-scripts must take pid and npid from the commandline.
    
3Aa For homogeneous islands:

    ./rdsRun.sh rdsTSPlin105Hom.R

    Results in directory rdsHomResult

3Ab For heterogeneous islands:

    ./rdsRun.sh rdsTSPlin105Het.R

    ./rdsRun.sh rdsTSPlin105HetAdapt.R

    ./rdsRun.sh rdsTSPlin105HetEarly.R 

    Results in directory rdsHetResult


3B. Start scripts in 4 terminals.

3Ba. For homogeneous islands:

    ./rdsTerminals.sh rdsTSPlin105Hom.R

3Bb. For heterogeneous islands:

    ./rdsTerminals.sh rdsTSPlin105Het.R

    ./rdsTerminals.sh rdsTSPlin105HetEarly.R

